WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.230
<b>Noukin High School Student Dorms</b>

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:10.140
In his Junior Youth era, up against 
all the powerhouse teams,

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:13.360
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined. 
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.240
he was never taken down once. 
A master of evasion.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.920
"Yoigoshi the Unstoppable."

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.740
<b>Under 15
Yoigoshi the Unstoppable
Rising Youth Kicker</b>

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.740
<b>How to get on the starting lineup</b>

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.740
Yoigoshi-kun! Perfect timing!

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.270
I'm the coach for the soccer team, Takenaka. 
Can we talk for a minute?

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.650
Is this an invite?

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.630
<b>Noukin High School, First-year
Yoigoshi Tatsuya</b>

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.570
Sorry, but I've already been forced 
to decide on a team.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.750
W-Wait, please!

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:35.630
Our soccer team absolutely needs 
"Yoigoshi the Unstoppable"!

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.510
<b>"Yoigoshi the Unstoppable"</b>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.510
"Unstoppable," huh?

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.640
When was that?

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.200
Yay!

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.220
<i>The kabaddi team.</i>

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.280
Men
\h\h\h\h\h\hWho Connect

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.490
<i>I have been forced to become a member.</i>

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.500
<b>Kabaddi Team First-Year
Azemichi Soma</b>

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:26.500
Yeah! Stopped the raid again!

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:29.170
Damn it! You musclebound morons!

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.920
No, I am still far from true muscularity.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.920
<b>Kabaddi Team Second-Year
Date Shinji</b>

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.920
Iura-san, why don't you let him 
practice some defense, too?

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.670
<b>Kabaddi Team Second-Year
Misumi Kyohei</b>

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.630
<b>Kabaddi Team Third-Year
Iura Kei</b>

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.930
Yes, well, I have been telling him 
he should work on some defense, but...

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.300
I refuse to do defense.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.060
Right, then!

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.310
We're on defense one more time!

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:48.150
Yeah!

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.060
Azemichi, you watch the mid-line!

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.570
<i>The offense in kabaddi, 
just like football and rugby,</i>

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.000
<i>gets targeted for tackles 
by a large number of players.</i>

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.480
<i>Even so, there is a reason 
I do not want to play defense.</i>

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.130
<i>And the reason is... this!</i>

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.660
<i>This incomprehensible formation 
where the defense hold hands!</i>

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.160
<i>I never, ever want to 
hold hands with other guys!</i>

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.400
What? You have some kind 
of aversion to holding hands?

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.940
They're rugged and hard,

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.200
but once you summon the courage 
and take hold, you'll soon get used to it.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.670
Stop talking about it that way!

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:23.700
Holding hands, or making a chain, 
is common practice in kabaddi defense.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.600
To counter a solo raider, 
you have a "pack" defense.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.710
When capturing a single, agile raider,

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:33.980
you need a "chain" to block 
their path or surround them.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.430
Chains, huh?

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:38.230
Sounds oppressive.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.010
<i>Ridiculous.</i>

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:43.840
<i>Connections with people should 
be light, like on the net.</i>

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.990
<b>Raider
Yoigoshi Tatsuya</b>

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:45.670
Kabaddi.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:47.990
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:47.990
<i>The basic rules of kabaddi are simple.</i>

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:52.540
<i>The offense chants "kabaddi" 
while entering the opponents' court.</i>

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.260
<i>If they can touch an opposing player 
and return to their side of the court,</i>

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.000
<i>they gain points.</i>

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.850
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.210
<i>But in actual practice, 
it can be surprisingly complex.</i>

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:05.930
<b>Defense
Iura Date Misumi</b>

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.790
<i>The raider is alone and 
the defense works as a pack...</i>

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:05.930
<i>It would be better to say 
that they're one giant animal.</i>

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:07.400
<i>After a touch, trying to return</i>

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.550
<i>to your territory down 
the middle is a fool's plan...</i>

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:13.690
<i>You'll end up surrounded on both sides.</i>

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.160
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:15.450
<i>Which means...</i>

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.590
<i>the one I should try to tag 
is the jerk with the perm!</i>

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:20.690
<i>I'll narrow down the chances 
for a tackle to the left side!</i>

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.210
<i>Even if the lightweight 
with the narrow eyes grabs me,</i>

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.700
Kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:24.700
<i>there is little danger 
of being taken down.</i>

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.700
Kabaddi!

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:26.700
<i>This should work.</i>

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.290
It was a good plan, but...

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.410
it was so good, it was easy to read.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:33.370
<i>He's so fast!</i>

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.420
<i>But for a raider, 
this is the same as a touch!</i>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.260
<i>If I can make it back to my 
territory, that's one point!</i>

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.670
Kabaddi...

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:40.840
You're not getting back!

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:41.730
We're not giving you a point!

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:43.720
Kabaddi...

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:48.550
<i>Oh! This... isn't good!</i>

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:55.520
This just shows that lighter guys 
can serve to slow you down.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.620
Next, we'll have Azemichi practice raiding.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.730
Sir!

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.730
<b>Raider
Azemichi Soma</b>

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.740
Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:11.830
Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:08.230
<i>Idiot. Shouting like that.</i>

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.830
<i>You only get to attack for as long 
as one breath lasts, you know?</i>

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:15.330
Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:15.330
<i>You're wasting oxygen. 
Get taken down like the fool you are.</i>

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.080
Kabaddi! Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.250
That'll never work.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:20.150
I couldn't even touch them, so you...

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:21.690
What?

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.550
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:24.830
We're in the struggle!

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:25.630
Stop him!

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:26.680
Don't let him get back!

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.480
Kabaddi! Kabaddi! Kabaddi—

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:33.350
Kabaddi! Kabaddi...

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:32.010
He's not stopping.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:39.810
<b>2nd-3rd-Years</b>

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:39.810
<b>Azemichi</b>

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.140
Raid successful!

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.660
And the struggle was with two people, 
so I get two points!

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:39.810
All right!

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:41.230
<i>How is this possible?!</i>

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:43.740
Were you watching the line, Yoigoshi?

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:45.310
Oh, uh, I have something in my eye...

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:46.900
Liar!

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:49.570
This is it. The kabaddi team.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:56.620
Gymnasium 1

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.750
I wish you, as head teacher, 
would try to persuade him, too.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.810
He should be playing soccer!

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.130
That's true.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.960
As you say, coach, for the 
sake of our school, he is-

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.140
It went in, I tell you! The tip!

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:02.170
Yeah, but after getting 
forced to the ground.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.920
Even if you're not upright, 
as long as it's in, it's in!

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.060
You are seriously such a tightass!

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:07.960
What?

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.510
You're the one who's satisfied 
with just the tip of one finger!

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:12.180
What kind of man are you?

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.680
Now, now. Yoigoshi, you try 
being the attacker again.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.830
Or would you rather come 
and hold hands with us?

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:18.810
I would not!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.510
Shall we try another day?

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:22.820
Yes, let's.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:29.750
I only managed a successful raid twice.

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:32.890
Yoigoshi, you didn't succeed 
even once, did you?

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:33.830
Don't worry about it.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:38.260
Since you're exhaling the whole time, 
raiding is tough, right?

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.080
Y-Yeah.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.920
After doing all that useless shouting, 
he should be more tired, but

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.090
he's succeeding at raids.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.220
Are you sure you're not 
taking it easy on him?

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:53.270
With Azemichi, he's doing 
so many unnecessary things,

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:54.660
it makes it harder for us.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:55.850
Huh?

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:58.020
<i>His being inefficient 
makes it harder to play him?</i>

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.270
<i>What is he talking about?</i>

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:02.770
<i>Now that I think about it, 
what did I used to do in soccer?</i>

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.770
<i>The basic method of evading 
opponents is the feint.</i>

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:08.250
<i>And to win,</i>

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:11.740
<i>you need to carefully observe 
the guys you can't stand.</i>

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.390
<i>The musclehead, Date.</i>

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:17.240
<i>He doesn't have speed, 
but he does have the most power.</i>

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:20.590
<i>If he catches me, even alone, 
it's a certain take-down.</i>

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.710
<i>I should try to avoid confronting him.</i>

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:24.860
<i>The jerk with the perm, Misumi.</i>

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:28.210
<i>He doesn't have the power Date does, 
but his reach is slightly longer.</i>

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:30.040
<i>He's the type that wants 
to go for the tackle.</i>

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.810
<i>It's a risk, but he's easier 
to mark for a touch.</i>

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:33.720
<i>And then...</i>

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:37.220
<i>the problem is the narrow-eyed guy, Iura.</i>

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.670
<i>He's got less speed and power than me, but</i>

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:42.300
<i>he can read movements, get ahead,
 and slow me down.</i>

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.760
<i>A real nuisance.</i>

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.730
<i>Think! How can I attack this?</i>

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:49.650
He's doing so many unnecessary things, 
it makes it harder for us.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.150
<i>That's it! I can see it!</i>

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:54.190
<i>A way to evade the chains!</i>

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:56.490
You look like you're thinking 
pretty hard there, Yoigoshi!

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.510
Quit being such a stranger! 
You can ask me about anything!

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:03.080
I mean, I am your senior 
in kabaddi, after all!

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:06.030
I have nothing to ask an idiot.

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:09.380
I'm sorry! I got a little cocky there.

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:11.430
Instead of talking about idiots and stuff,

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:12.940
we could, you know, talk about kabaddi—

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:15.590
But there was something 
to be learned from an idiot.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.200
I won't lose this time.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.490
Did you find some surefire way to win?

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:21.840
Tell me! Tell me!

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.100
An idiot wouldn't be able to do it.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:28.170
An idio— I won't know until I try!

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.660
Okay! Break's over!

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:35.800
We'll split into defense and offense. 
Yoigoshi is raiding first.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:37.970
Azemichi, you be referee, okay?

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:38.870
Sir!

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:42.600
Keep your guard up.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:46.260
It seems Yoigoshi has 
some kind of secret plan.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.960
That's right.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:52.920
Let me show you my hat trick!

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:55.930
Hat trick?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:58.450
What's a "hat trick"?

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:02.060
In soccer, it's when a single player 
scores three goals in one game.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:04.480
<i>This is a bluff.</i>

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.500
<i>The risks of touching all 
three of us are too high.</i>

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:12.450
<i>To get three points, he'd have to 
lure us in, let himself get caught,</i>

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:14.090
<i>and, in that moment, 
return to his territory.</i>

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.580
<i>Touching us each individually is too risky,</i>

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.540
<i>and his breath wouldn't 
last long enough anyway.</i>

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:21.960
<i>No, wait...</i>

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:26.120
<i>With that bluff, we'd all be careful 
not to get lured too close together.</i>

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:30.670
<b>Raider
Yoigoshi Tatsuya</b>

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:28.710
<i>That could be what Yoigoshi is aiming for.</i>

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:34.170
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:34.670
<i>A sort of feint to keep himself 
from being easily tackled.</i>

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.220
Kabaddi!

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:37.430
<i>Good!</i>

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.650
<i>Even when I step in some, 
they aren't coming to grab me.</i>

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:41.220
<i>The diversion is working!</i>

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:45.040
I don't dislike a cunning plan.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:55.820
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.190
I'll keep it to myself, though.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:50.870
<i>This guy... Has he noticed 
the trap I've set?</i>

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:54.510
<i>But, I noticed something, too. 
The reason I lose...</i>

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:56.720
<i>The difference between Azemichi and myself.</i>

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.740
Kabaddi. Kabaddi!

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:01.880
<i>The cant. Repeating "kabaddi" over and over.</i>

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:09.000
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:04.440
If it stops, the raid fails.

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:09.000
<i>It's more important to keep a 
constant volume than to be loud, but...</i>

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:13.540
<i>my voice only gets louder 
when I go in for a touch.</i>

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:15.010
Kabaddi!

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:27.020
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.980
<i>Which means they were using 
my cant to read my movements</i>

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:19.570
<i>and get ahead of me!</i>

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.560
<i>Keep the cant steady.</i>

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:23.800
<i>That alone will help to keep them 
from reading me,</i>

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:26.320
<i>but I'm going to deliberately 
make my cant unsteady...</i>

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.810
<i>and use it as a feint!</i>

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:35.690
<i>Did he read me?</i>

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.570
<i>Targeting me was your mistake.</i>

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:44.240
<i>The cant should hold steady naturally, 
like breathing in yoga.</i>

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.340
<i>Realizing that and deliberately 
going for the opposite...</i>

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.290
<i>That kind of twisted thinking... 
is something I do, too.</i>

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:53.790
It was fun... your two-layered trap.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.960
But that isn't enough to escape the chain—

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.420
You're in the struggle!

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.590
<i>What? I haven't touched him yet—</i>

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:03.160
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:05.600
<i>His foot?</i>

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:11.100
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:08.420
<i>He was targeting Date from the start?</i>

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.100
<i>It isn't a two-layered trap. 
I told you, didn't I?</i>

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:13.780
<i>This will break through the chain...</i>

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:18.000
<i>a triple-layer trap, the hat trick!</i>

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:18.780
Stop him!

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:22.280
<i>I kicked him with my return leg. 
There's no way you're catching me!</i>

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:27.490
<i>Did you see that? My first win!</i>

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.420
Kaba—

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:30.900
<i>You can't be serious!</i>

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:33.920
Yoigoshi!

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.700
You okay? That was a huge noise.

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:40.530
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:43.470
<i>I stopped my cant, but I haven't 
made it back to my territory yet!</i>

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:51.350
Be more careful about your shoelaces.

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:53.980
Yeah. It won't be a problem.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:57.480
It's been a while since I tripped 
on my own. I was surprised is all.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:01.320
But, who'd have thought you'd go 
for a touch with your feet.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:05.570
Did you really make it back 
to your territory? I couldn't tell.

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:08.470
O-Of course I did!

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:09.530
I definitely—

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:11.050
You were in.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:16.920
Finally, right? Little by little... 
he made it in.

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:19.940
What's with the weird phrasing?

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:23.430
If that's the ref's call, 
there's nothing else to say.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:26.890
But, it looks like you need 
to get some proper shoes.

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:30.890
Let's see... Tomorrow, after school.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:35.330
We'll all go together to buy 
kabaddi shoes for Yoigoshi.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:39.480
It will serve well both for safety 
and to deepen our friendship, right?

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:43.560
We can call it "The Kabaddi 
Team Friendship Shopping Plan"!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:44.940
Nice!

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:47.550
The name of the plan is very literal.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:49.490
I'm super looking forward to it!

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:53.420
Shopping... with these guys?

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:02.630
Okay.

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:06.640
So, tomorrow, after school, 
we'll come get you.

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:09.410
<i>I'll go home before they get here.</i>

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:12.020
<i>I don't want to go shopping 
with guys like them.</i>

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.310
Let's go!

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:22.720
Careful on your way home!

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:23.530
Yes, sir.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.410
So you play the nice guy out here, huh?

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:28.150
It's not a bad thing, is it?

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.400
Besides, there are a lot 
of powerhouse sports teams here,

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.610
so we need to make 
as many friends as we can.

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:37.040
Otherwise, our team budget 
and position will be in danger.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:40.600
Well, we don't have many members, 
and we are playing kabaddi, after all.

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:43.920
<i>A team bag?</i>

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.220
<i>It's so ugly.</i>

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:49.190
Don't worry! We'll make one 
for you, too, Yoigoshi!

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:51.820
S-Sorry for making a show 
of them in front of you.

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:53.220
It's not like I want one!

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.910
But, they make you really feel like 
we're friends! Aren't they great?

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:58.730
It's proof we're a team!

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:04.480
Even with the same bag and uniform, 
sometimes you aren't a team.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:05.960
Huh?

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:08.350
At any rate, I hate all this 
"trying to get along" stuff.

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:09.980
It's irritating.

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:14.470
You say that, but you're very diligent 
about coming to practice, aren't you?

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:17.600
Speaking of which, Yoigoshi, 
you haven't done any livestreams lately.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:18.450
Huh?

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:21.130
If I weren't stuck with you guys, 
I'd do one in a flash.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:24.380
Even though livestreamers get flamed a lot?

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:27.010
If you tried it, you'd see why it's fun.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.260
"If you tried it," huh?

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:30.390
What?

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:34.980
I was just thinking 
that kabaddi is the same way.

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:43.050
They're selling more kinds than I expected.

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:45.360
We'll use the team budget to buy them, 
so make sure to choose well.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.540
They're playing footage from a tournament!

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:49.810
Wow!

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.750
This shape is like those other ones...

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.900
You see them in combat sports, right?

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:55.990
Kabaddi has the same form as a combat sport.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:58.390
The closest is wrestling.

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:02.580
So, a thin sole and tall ankle 
is probably the most common design.

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:06.640
Enough people play 
that they can hold tournaments?

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:09.360
I thought of it as a bit 
of gag sport, but...

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:13.420
Well, it doesn't compare to the 
major sports. It's pretty small-scale.

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:17.570
It makes guys like our senpais 
who have played forever very happy.

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:19.060
Senpais... plural?

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:21.970
We have one more third-year.

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:23.060
Oh...

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.570
I see. It's a tough world, huh?

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:27.650
Huh?

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:34.600
Because it's a minor sport, 
there aren't as many opportunities,

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:36.600
so there are a ton of 
desperate players, right?

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:40.690
It wasn't the same field, but I fought a bunch
 of different kinds of guys at nationals.

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:44.590
Whether it was a powerhouse or a weak team,

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:48.090
the most difficult ones to play 
were the desperate ones.

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:53.960
That hurts to hear. I mean, 
I underestimated them, at first, right?

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:56.600
And we always lose in the first round.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:59.400
<i>The "desperate ones," huh?</i>

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:01.620
<i>Now I think about it, 
no matter how much he complains,</i>

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:04.100
<i>I've never seen Yoigoshi slack off.</i>

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:06.530
But, it seems like a real waste.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:09.260
Quitting when you're at the national level.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:11.020
Why did you quit soccer?

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:13.070
Why?

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:15.640
Why don't you pass to me?

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:17.790
I'm running out in front!

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:22.080
You're always racing ahead on your own,

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:25.790
at a speed where we can't catch up.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.520
Yoigoshi?

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:37.110
I already told you. 
I've always hated sports.

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:41.460
Yoigoshi. Are you gonna
 buy those shoes?

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:44.130
Huh? What're you grinning about?

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:47.510
Well, it's just that those 
are the same as the ones I bought!

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:50.030
Why are you putting them back?!

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:54.490
<i>Okay. I guess I'll get these.</i>

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.960
<i>Where did Iura run off to?</i>

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:01.790
Hold on! One more time!

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:06.590
Come on, one hundred fifty kilos!

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:08.150
<i>They're from our basketball team?</i>

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:13.000
Huh? Hey, if it isn't Yoigoshi!

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:15.760
What's this? Shopping?

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.640
<i>Who's this? Acting all familiar.</i>

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:20.450
So the rumors are true, huh?

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:21.140
Rumors?

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:25.050
They say the soccer genius 
has joined some weird team.

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:29.340
I don't really know much, but it's "kabaddi." 
That hilarious one, right?

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:33.850
Is kabaddi actually an impressive 
sport or something?

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:35.350
Hey, look at that! Look!

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:36.370
See the bag?

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:38.740
That little cueball must be
 in the kabaddi club, too!

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:41.580
He's tiny! What a total joke!

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:46.450
Hey, Azemichi. Come here a minute.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:49.440
Let's have a match. I found something fun.

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:50.250
Sure.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.380
This measures the strength of your back.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.070
It says the average 
for a high school first-year is...

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:57.400
about one hundred forty kilos.

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:59.000
I just pull, right?

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:03.940
What? You're going to 
go up against him with this?

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:05.950
You shouldn't pick on the weak, you know—

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.510
T-Two hundred?!

00:18:09.510 --> 00:18:11.020
Are you a pro wrestler or something?

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:14.030
You want to have a go, too?

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:18.030
N-No, thank you. We're fine.

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:21.620
Don't diss.

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:28.070
It says I got two hundred fourteen 
kilos! Your turn, Yoigoshi!

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:31.180
Huh? We're done with that. 
I feel all refreshed.

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:33.040
You said we were having a match!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:36.050
If you don't do it, I'll look 
like an idiot all on my own!

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:44.560
You are an idiot.

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.790
I am not an idiot!

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.740
The kabaddi team's insane.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:52.580
You there, can I have a moment?

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:55.220
Huh? Who are you?

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:00.190
Hey.

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:00.890
Yes?

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:04.010
Those basketball guys were being 
super polite when we left.

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:05.080
What did you do?

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.580
Thank you for all your hard work!

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.440
Oh, nothing.

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:12.120
I just told them a little secret, that's all.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:13.980
Like when we talked about livestreaming.

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:15.000
<i>This guy...</i>

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:18.640
They said they'd help us look 
for new members!

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:21.680
We need seven members.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.680
When you don't have 
enough people on defense,

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.010
it makes it hard to train on offense.

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:28.730
If only Yoigoshi could play defense.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:31.420
If I don't have to hold hands, 
I don't mind doing it.

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:32.650
Right?

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:34.900
You're kidding! What happened to you?

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:35.880
Should we call an ambulance?

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:37.650
I'm not sick or hurt or anything!

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:39.780
It's just...

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.860
I can't stand getting beaten 
by that guy all the time.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:47.790
Until I can win, I'll get 
a little more serious about this.

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:53.370
You really are a sore loser, aren't you?

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:59.220
It's a text from a girl in my class.

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:02.220
"Will you introduce me to Yoigoshi-kun?"
 is what she wrote.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:04.970
This is the first time I've seen one of these.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:07.470
Oh, you little lady-killer!

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:11.160
Oh, yeah. Yoigoshi, you got a girlfriend?

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:13.480
They only get in the way.

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:16.260
We've got so many bachelors here, it's sad.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:18.510
Misumi broke up recently, right?

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:21.610
Boring. So, the only one 
with a girlfriend is...

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:25.110
you, huh, Azemichi?

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:27.160
Huh?

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.000
A girl out in the countryside, right?

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:31.580
You may be far apart, but make sure 
you treasure your girlfriend, okay?

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.170
Sir! I'll do my best!

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:37.530
<i>N-No... It's not like...</i>

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:39.710
<i>It's not unnatural, or anything.</i>

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:41.890
<i>For Azemichi to have a girlfriend, that's...</i>

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:43.840
<i>Having a girlfriend, I mean, that's...</i>

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:46.650
<i>I've never had one, but if I wanted one, 
I could have one right away anyway.</i>

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:49.080
<i>I'm not upset about this at all!</i>

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.030
<i>It's not at all like he's passed me up,</i>

00:20:51.030 --> 00:20:54.110
<i>but I should check and see 
if he really does have a girlfriend.</i>

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:55.230
<i>That's only right!</i>

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:59.230
D-Do you have a picture 
of your girlfriend?

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:01.100
I do, but...

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.170
It's sort of embarrassing.

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:04.360
I will kill you.

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:06.910
What are you angry about?

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.160
Just show me.

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:11.120
Here. This is her.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.680
<i>It's not important.</i>

00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:17.360
<i>It's the kind of girl who would 
date a guy like him.</i>

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.960
<i>She's probably a cow reeking of potato—</i>

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:26.840
Die!

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:27.820
Why?!

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:28.540
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:30.130
Calm down, Yoigoshi!

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:31.930
I was shocked at first, too, but...

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:33.510
Don't try to stop me!

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:37.300
For the sake of all men, 
I will kill him here and now!

00:21:37.300 --> 00:21:39.230
What kind of sense of duty is that?

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:44.280
Coach, are you serious?

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:47.550
You're both handsome. And you're tall!

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:48.500
You'll be fine!

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:50.530
Fine with what, Coach?

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:52.490
You! You!

00:21:51.190 --> 00:21:54.120
What are you so angry about?

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:54.120
They're here. Go!

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:55.810
I'm talking about breaking up!

00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:57.250
Long-distance relationships never work!

00:21:57.250 --> 00:22:00.460
And with that height, 
I'm a better match anyway, right?

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:04.020
I'm not breaking up with her! 
Size has nothing to do with anything!

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:07.100
Size matters!

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:07.100
A l-lovers' quarrel!

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:10.990
I see. So, that's his type.

00:22:10.990 --> 00:22:12.220
I'll have to try again.

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:18.040
<i>And so, the curtain closed on 
"The Kabaddi Team Friendship Shopping Plan."</i>

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:54.430
<b>Next Time|
"Into the Burning World"</b>

00:23:49.250 --> 00:23:52.270
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:49.690 --> 00:23:50.700
Next time...

00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:52.270
"Into the Burning World"!

00:23:52.270 --> 00:23:53.370
Kabaddi!
